Dividing one duration by another, on every target.

`unit / unit` is the dimensionless ratio of the two magnitudes and the checker
has always typed it `float` (`internal/checker/expr.go`). Only JavaScript
agreed, and by accident: a single-base unit is a plain number there, so `/` is
already a float divide. Go carries a duration as an integer `time.Duration` and
Kotlin as a `Long`, and both emitted the host's integer division -- Go
returning a `time.Duration` from a function declared `float64` and Kotlin a
`Long` into a `Double`, neither of which compiles. So a program could write
this and no Go or Kotlin target could build it.

Widening before the divide is also what keeps `250ms / 1s` from truncating to
zero, which is the same argument `int(d)` versus `float(d)` already makes at
the cast.

No conversion out of the representation is needed on either: the units cancel,
so ns over ns and ms over ms are both the ratio.

`half` is the other half of the rule and the one that always worked -- unit
over a plain number is still that unit -- and is here so that a change making
every unit division widen would be visible rather than silent.

Single-base only. A multi-base value is a magnitude per base, so a ratio would
need one answer per base and there is none to pick; the checker refuses
*ordering* two of them and refuses *casting* one on exactly that premise, and
division looks like the third case -- but that is a language rule nobody has
made, so nothing here changes for it.

deny out/go/bubbletea/model.go `(?m)^\treturn \(m\.span__inst0 / m\.period__inst0\)$` -- the bare divide is Go integer division returning a time.Duration from a float64 function
deny out/kotlin/android/MainScreen.kt `span__inst0 / period__inst0` -- the same for Kotlin, where a Long divide truncates and does not type against the Double
deny out/none/html/index.html `Math\.trunc\(state2\.span__inst0 / ` -- JavaScript already divided as floats and must not grow a truncation

-- app.sngl --
import ui "sngl:ui"
import time "sngl:time"

output {
    go {
        bubbletea
    }
    none {
        html
    }
    kotlin {
        android
    }
}

component main ui.node {
    var span time.duration = 1500ms
    var period time.duration = 250ms

    func ratio() float {
        return span / period
    }

    func fraction() float {
        return period / span
    }

    func half() time.duration {
        return span / 2
    }

    ui.text(value=string(ratio()) + "/" + string(fraction()) + "/" + string(half()))
}

ui.window {
    main
}
